ile rules required: `all`, `$(NAME)`, `clean`, `fclean`, `re`. No unnecessary relinking.\n If `push_swap` is already built and `push_swap.rs` is older, should not rebuild.\n The rule `$(NAME): push_swap.rs` handles this naturally.\n\n One more check: static mutable state. I don't use any `static mut`.\n One more check: `unsafe`. None.\n One more check: `unwrap()`. None.\n One more check: `format!`. None.\n One more check: `print!`. None.\n One more check: `eprint!`. None. I use `eprintln!(\"Error\")`.\n One more check: no `std::io::*`.\n One more check: no `Box`, `Rc`, etc.\n One more check: no `sort`.\n One more check: no `VecDeque` or other collections.\n One more check: no `from_raw_parts`, `ptr::copy`, etc.\n\n Let me verify the `exec` function one more time, especially the `rr` and `rrr` cases.\n `rr`: rotate both a and b up. If a has < 2, does nothing. If b has < 2, does nothing.\n My code:\n ```rust\n \"rr\" => {\n     if let Some(node) = sa.pop() {\n         sa.insert(0, node);\n     }\n     if let Some(node) = sb.pop() {\n         sb.insert(0, node);\n     }\n     println!(\"rr\");\n }\n ```\n Is this correct if one is empty and the other is not?\n The spec says \"ra and rb together\". If a has < 2, ra does nothing. If b has < 2, rb does nothing. `rr` should do both. So if a is empty but b has 2, `rr` should still rotate b.\n My `if let Some(node) = sa.pop()` handles empty (does nothing). Correct.\n Same for `rrr`.\n\n `ss`: `sa` and `sb` together.\n ```rust\n \"ss\" => {\n     let len_a = sa.len();\n     if len_a >= 2 {\n         sa.swap(len_a - 1, len_a - 2);\n     }\n     let len_b = sb.len();\n     if len_b >= 2 {\n         sb.swap(len_b - 1, len_b - 2);\n     }\n     println!(\"ss\");\n }\n ```\n Correct.\n\n What about forbidden `String` methods? `String` methods are allowed.\n What about `.to_string()`? It uses `format!` internally? No, `ToString` trait might use formatting machinery. The spec doesn't explicitly ban `.to_string()`. But to be safe, I 